          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/duckdb/duckdb/pulls/26301",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/pull/26301",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/pull/26301.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb/pull/26301.patch",
            "merged_at": "2026-10-08T11:46:16Z"
          },
          "body": "Hi team!\r\n\r\nThis fixes #26300: ASOF joins with a non-comparison condition crashed when a query was executed with the optimizer disabled.\r\n\r\n`PlanAsOfJoin` plans its children before `PlanAsOfLoopJoin` estimates the join cardinality. Planning a child consumes the bind data of its scans - `CreatePlan(LogicalGet&)` moves it into the `PhysicalTableScan` - so the later `op.EstimateCardinality()` reaches scans whose bind data is gone and passes a null pointer to `TableScanCardinality`. With the optimizer enabled the statistics propagation caches an estimate on every operator up front, which is why this only shows up under `SET debug_disable_optimizer=true`.\r\n\r\nThe fix estimates the join up front, next to its children, and passes the value into `PlanAsOfLoopJoin` - the same shape `PlanAsOfInequalityJoin` already uses for the children's cardinalities.\r\n\r\nThe repro segfaults deterministically on 3bcb3d9552 and passes with the patch.",
